<!--
    The shape of a journey ridden on one's own bike (SPEC §7.3).

    The same drawing as `illustration_journey`, with the middle taken out: two
    discs — where one stands, where one is going — and one unbroken stroke
    between them. No station disc in between, because none is used; no dashes,
    because nothing is walked. The eye reads the difference from the other
    illustration without reading the sentence above it.

    The two discs are the filled bike disc the interface already draws, where
    the other illustration's ends are outlined and bear a walking figure: the
    figure inside a disc says how that point is lived, and nobody walks any of
    this journey. The bike is the plain one, whatever the network lends — the
    bolt and the cog say what waits at a station (SPEC §15).

    Mirrored in right-to-left languages, for the reason the other one gives.
-->
